WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.150
Attention, all mechanics:

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:21.450
Henhouse work will begin
promptly at 1400 hours.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.830
Bring your 104 equipment.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:30.420
No-shows can expect to
have all 405 privileges suspended.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:47.890
<i>Man cannot live by bread alone.</i>

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:58.650
<i>But the stuff of life allows us</i>
<i>to pursue the finer things.</i>

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:04.700
<i>Although there is more to life</i>
<i>than simply scrambling for food,</i>

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.290
<i>it remains an undeniable necessity.</i>

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.580
<i>And since the police must be</i>
<i>ready for any circumstance,</i>

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.880
<i>for us, good sustenance</i>
<i>helps fulfill two sacred duties:</i>

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:23.010
<i>Maintaining body and soul</i>
<i>in peak condition,</i>

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:29.350
<i>which allows us to stay</i>
<i>highly focused on our mission.</i>

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.610
<i>Man ignores his culinary</i>
<i>requirements only at great peril.</i>

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.530
<i>This report details that sad truth.</i>

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:44.280
<i>It is a record of the terrors</i>
<i>which struck Second Section.</i>

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:55.790
<i>The police enforce man's law,</i>
<i>but nature's law is far harsher.</i>

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:03.050
<i>These events prove that.</i>

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.720
<i>But it all began simply enough...</i>

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:13.520
The Destruction of Special
Vehicles, Second Section!

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.310
Hey, it's almost lunchtime, Noa.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.780
What? Lunchtime already?

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:21.740
Get me wonton and gyoza.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.700
Wonton and gyoza.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.790
A large yakiniku bowl.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.500
The number 5 noodle bowl.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.620
Miso ramen and rice.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.540
A large Chinese noodles.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.460
Large noodles and wonton.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.170
Fried noodles and a large rice.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.340
Large curry rice, no pickles.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.300
Stuffed green pepper and rice.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:52.430
Noodles, miso ramen, rice, large
Chinese noodles, another...?

00:04:54.940 --> 00:05:00.730
Chinese noodles, wonton,
fried noodles, large rice, curry rice.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.150
I have this.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.900
Homemade bento. How nice.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:10.030
Miss Izumi, I made rice balls.
Do you want one?

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.370
Thank you. I'll have one later.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.040
Bowl of noodles, PLEASE!

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.000
A large butter-corn ramen
and a side of rice.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.710
Large Chinese bowl.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:24.090
Fried beef and rice with garlic.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.680
Same thing. Fried beef
and rice, no garlic.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.760
Katsudon, extra large.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.760
Shrimp fried rice, side of ramen.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.720
A large bowl of Chinese noodles.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.930
Ramen and gyoza rice.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.900
Let's see...

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.320
Chinese noodles and a side of rice.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.360
I'll have shrimp fried rice.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:53.410
Shanghai Restaurant? This is
Second Section, with our order.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:06:00.790
Let's see, wonton, gyoza,
large yakiniku, and uh...

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.340
Hello?

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:13.470
Wonton and gyoza, right?
I remember the first two.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.520
If you remember then get going!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.230
A large yakiniku!

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:22.020
The number 5 noodle bowl.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.690
Miso ramen and rice.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.110
Large Chinese noodles.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.150
Large noodles and wonton.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.360
Fried noodles and a large rice.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.910
Large curry rice, hold the pickles.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.830
Stuffed green pepper and rice.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.540
Bowl of noodles, PLEASE!

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:43.500
I had a butter-corn ramen,
but change it to egg-drop soup.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.710
I was the Chinese bowl,
but now I want katsudon.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:51.340
Fried beef and rice with garlic.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.430
Same thing. Fried beef
and rice, no garlic.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.310
Change my large katsudon to tempura.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.850
I'm still fried rice and ramen.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.810
I still want Chinese noodles.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.020
Ramen and gyoza rice.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.900
Once I decide, I never change my mind.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:08.940
Same here.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.910
This is Second Section,
with today's order.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:21.580
Two wontons, gyoza, yakiniku,
number 5 noodles, noodles,

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:26.670
miso ramen, rice, Chinese noodles,
large noodles and wonton...

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:31.430
...egg-drop soup, large katsudon,
two fried beef, tempura,

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:38.470
two shrimp bowls, large Chinese
noodles, ramen, gyoza rice,

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.520
half order of rice, and that's it.
Thank you!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:45.520
Tsutomu, I've told you before:
No food until your work is done!

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.290
They're late.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:09.000
I love you

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.480
Shanghai restaurant?
What are you waiting for?

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.850
Are you trying to kill us?

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.190
Look, we're doing our best.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.730
You know, it's faster if
you all order the same thing.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.940
We order from you every
day of the year!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:36.320
If we didn't have some
variety, we'd go nuts!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.320
Tsutomu!

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:41.870
If there's time to gab,
there's time to scrub!

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.630
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.170
<i>But the delivery never arrived.</i>

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.800
<i>Lunch hour ended, but</i>
<i>no one returned to work.</i>

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:07.730
<i>It slowly became apparent that no</i>
<i>delivery would EVER be coming.</i>

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:12.780
There are limits to our patience!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.400
He already left.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.490
I told you... he's on his way.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.740
You're young.
A late lunch won't kill you.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.830
Quit whining and be patient.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:35.170
Listen, everyone! Our delivery
has just left the restaurant!

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:43.350
Just once, my friends, let us believe
the Shanghai's claim!

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:49.230
We'll give them another 30 minutes...
but no longer!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:52.440
And if our food hasn't arrived by then,

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.360
we'll take matters into our OWN hands!

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.900
All units, stand by.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:06.000
<i>And so, Second Section</i>
<i>waited eagerly for their delivery.</i>

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.330
<i>And 30 minutes passed.</i>

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:15.050
<i>And then another 30 minutes passed.</i>
<i>Still, there was no food.</i>

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.140
I'm warning you, don't
make me lose my temper!

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:27.100
That's odd. Tsutomu never arrived?
Now I'm getting worried.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:32.310
Who cares about you?
What about our food?

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.520
But Tsutomu isn't...

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:38.110
I don't care about your problems!

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.450
YOU can bring the food!

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:45.910
But we shut off the burners
after lunch. The grill is cold.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:49.620
So you're refusing to fill our order?

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:53.380
Then we will never order from you again!

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:01.470
What did you do that for?
What are we going to do now?

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.390
No one else is stupid
enough to deliver out here!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.720
Shut up! Don't confuse the issue!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.310
I <i>told</i> you not to let Ota talk to him.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:11.650
No you didn't.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:13.150
Are you going to apologize?

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.940
Apologize?

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:20.530
Damn you, I'd rather die first!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:26.950
You brought a lunch! How can you
understand our suffering?

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.370
Let me go, you fools!

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.040
I can't stand it anymore!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:35.000
They've been exploiting us!

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:38.380
Yeah! Haven't the portions
been getting smaller?

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.130
I'm starting to feel weak!

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:42.930
Gentlemen!

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.220
The negotiations have broken down.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.970
The delivery... won't be coming.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:56.360
We are now on hostile terms
with the Shanghai Restaurant!

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:07.160
<i>If only we had accepted</i>
<i>our fate and moved on.</i>

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:14.080
<i>But the Shanghai is the only</i>
<i>restaurant near Second Section,</i>

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:18.550
<i>so our young heroes</i>
<i>couldn't give up on it.</i>

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.800
You pathetic wimps!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.970
Young people ought to
skip a meal, now and then!

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:28.930
When I was your age, I worked
so hard that I forgot to eat!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.930
But Sir, things are different nowadays.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:38.060
Shut up! You slackers
could stand a little deprivation!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.900
I'm going to HQ with Captain Nagumo.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.200
Quit your bellyaching
and get back to work!

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.670
Goodbye, Sir!

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.880
A full belly can create a cruel master.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:11.560
<i>Can a healthy man truly</i>
<i>understand his ailing comrades?</i>

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:16.730
<i>It is hunger which leads</i>
<i>to mankind's greatest sorrows.</i>

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:20.020
<i>And so the run of bad luck began.</i>

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.990
<i>The convenience store</i>
<i>was closed for renovation,</i>

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.950
<i>the fish wouldn't bite,</i>

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.280
<i>the rice had run out,</i>

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.370
<i>the hens had stopped laying eggs,</i>

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:44.340
<i>and the tomatoes, harvested</i>
<i>just last week, were now gone.</i>

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.340
<i>The strain on the men</i>
<i>approached the breaking point.</i>

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:56.560
Maybe you should apologize.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.520
Shanghai Restaurant.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.860
This is Ota, Special Vehicles.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.320
You sound pretty good
for a starving man. What's up?

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.160
I retract my statement.
Now will you deliver to us?

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.740
Huh? What are you trying to say?

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:15.250
I take back that I called you a
COMPLETE IDIOT!

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.540
I'm sorry, Sir.
Officer Ota is very, very sorry.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.170
Well, okay. What's your order?

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.550
One moment please.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.170
Wonton and gyoza.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:30.340
A large yakiniku bowl...
make it medium rare.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:35.060
The number 5 noodle bowl...
no green peas, plus wonton.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:37.640
Ramen and large rice.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.310
A large Chinese noodles.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.020
Large noodles and wonton.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.270
Fried noodles and a large rice.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:47.690
Large curry rice, hold
the pickles, add a raw egg.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:50.990
Stuffed green pepper,
large rice, and a ramen.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.950
Fried rice.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.870
I had an egg-drop soup,

00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:00.170
but make it a large butter-corn
ramen and 3 bowls of rice.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.630
I had the large Chinese bowl,
but now I want katsudon.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:10.760
Fried beef and rice with garlic,
and three eggs.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:15.010
Same thing, but a large,
and five eggs.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.060
Large katsudon.
No, make it tempura.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.270
Shrimp bowl, side of ramen.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.730
A large bowl of Chinese noodles.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.190
Ramen and gyoza rice.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.370
Get me whatever.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:39.080
What? You can't deliver? But-

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:42.290
Tsutomu never came back.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.250
And there are so many vicious
stray dogs in your neighborhood.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.380
Give me that!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:49.210
You jerk! How dare you lead us on?

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:52.590
That was your plan,
wasn't it, you fiend!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:56.890
So you're afraid of dogs?
How about if we ESCORT you?

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.970
Yeah, sure. That would work.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.680
We'll be right there!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.110
We don't have to do this.

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.400
Shut up!

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:14.320
Machine 2, heading out
to escort a Shanghai delivery!

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:15.780
Good luck!

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.700
Thanks a lot!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.540
Bring us noodles!

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.790
Don't forget mine!

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.040
Are you sure this will be okay?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.500
I fear the wrath of starving men.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.420
<i>Everyone shared Ota's outrage.</i>

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.220
<i>Not even the Captain could</i>
<i>have stopped things now.</i>

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:36.760
<i>And so, the doomed</i>
<i>expedition set forth.</i>

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:41.230
<i>But it never returned.</i>

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:47.110
Come in machine 2!
This is car 1.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.860
Where are you, machine 2?
Answer me, Ota!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.570
Something's wrong...

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:56.200
We can't just leave them.
We'd better go check.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.030
Let's go, Noa.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:02.620
Shige, mind the shop.
If HQ calls...

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:05.500
Don't worry. I know what to say.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.220
Hello, Special Ve... Hey, Shige!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:23.230
Shinshi? What happened?
The Captain's coming to -

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:29.270
Ota... I... You mustn't come!

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:30.980
Shinshi?

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.780
Won... ton... noodles!

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.110
Shinshi! Shinshi!

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.410
Shige?

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.740
Get ready! We're heading to the
Shanghai Restaurant!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.210
Second Section mechanics: MOVE OUT!

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:05.480
<i>But they never returned, either.</i>

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.400
<i>So finally, it was my turn.</i>

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.440
<i>What had happened to my teammates?</i>

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:17.030
<i>Now, I would share their dreadful fate.</i>

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.480
Special Vehicles Team Destroyed!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.940
Mass Food Poisoning!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:53.150
Colossal
Blunder!

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:58.360
<i>The truth is often surprisingly simple.</i>

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:02.700
<i>In retrospect, it's all due to our</i>
<i>unique circumstances.</i>

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:07.410
<i>Every day, we place a huge order with</i>
<i>the Shanghai restaurant.</i>

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:14.340
<i>Every day, the delivery man</i>
<i>has a huge amount of work.</i>

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:18.840
<i>This day, owner Hayao Sakimiya,</i>
<i>age 51, gave a strong reprimand,</i>

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.640
<i>to delivery man Tsutomu</i>
<i>Uchiyama, age 22.</i>

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:29.140
<i>In revenge, Tsutomu simply rode off.</i>

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:36.190
<i>The owner, learning that</i>
<i>Tsutomu had never arrived,</i>

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:43.700
<i>finally located his missing cart.</i>

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:51.120
<i>The tragedy was that he didn't know</i>
<i>where the food had gone.</i>

00:19:54.790 --> 00:20:00.380
<i>Following Ota's call, the owner</i>
<i>prepared new meals,</i>

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:05.930
<i>but there was no time to wash the</i>
<i>contaminated dishes.</i>

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:10.020
<i>When Ota and Shinshi arrived,</i>
<i>they began to eat.</i>

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:14.100
<i>The food poisoning struck, soon after.</i>

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:19.400
<i>Through sheer willpower, Officer</i>
<i>Shinshi tried to call in a warning,</i>

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:25.370
<i>but since the Captain had just left,</i>
<i>it only led to further tragedy.</i>

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.540
Shinshi? Shinshi?

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.580
<i>The shop owner fled in terror.</i>

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:42.260
<i>Captain Goto found his men</i>
<i>unconscious, and removed them.</i>

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:47.800
<i>He called the base before</i>
<i>heading to the hospital,</i>

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:54.440
<i>but the mechanics had already gone.</i>

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:57.110
Let's go, team!

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:07.280
<i>And so the second wave arrived.</i>

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:12.290
<i>They found the shop mysteriously empty,</i>
<i>filled with hot food.</i>

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.960
<i>It was like finding the</i> Marie Celeste,
<i>mysteriously abandoned.</i>

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:21.420
<i>And the scene that</i>
<i>followed should be obvious.</i>

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.050
Let's eat!

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.840
My noodles!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.010
That's my ramen!

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.100
Where's my fried rice?

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:29.970
Delicious!

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:34.180
<i>And thus was Special Vehicles,</i>
<i>Second Section utterly defeated.</i>

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:41.820
<i>This is another shameful blot on</i>
<i>Second Section's pitiful history.</i>

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.570
<i>Now you know the full story</i>
<i>behind this wretched tale.</i>

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:47.660
<i>It's been three weeks.</i>

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:52.290
<i>The shop owner slunk back,</i>
<i>and everyone made a full recovery.</i>

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:56.500
<i>If we can take one lesson</i>
<i>from this disaster, it is this:</i>

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:03.420
<i>Never again can we be</i>
<i>dependent on one restaurant.</i>

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:09.930
<i>Second Section must be ready</i>
<i>to face the next culinary crisis.</i>

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:18.850
<i>This was merely a wake-up call,</i>
<i>to future dietary disasters.</i>

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:24.230
Miss Kumagami, what'll it be today?

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:26.990
Wonton noodles, please.

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:29.570
And hold the onions.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:33.530
Mamoru, I've told you before:
No food until your work is done!

